# YouSim needs almost no configuration.
#
#   yousim connect     # links an OpenRouter account via OAuth, nothing to paste
#   yousim             # go
#
# That stores your key under ~/.yousim (macOS Keychain where available, a 0600
# file otherwise) and there is nothing else to set. `yousim config` prints what
# is in effect and which layer each value came from.
#
# ─── ./.env is NOT read ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A file named .env in the current directory is deliberately ignored, and any
# value Bun already loaded from one is discarded at startup.
#
# .env is an ambient convention: it exists in countless repos for reasons that
# have nothing to do with this tool. Honoring it would mean `cd` into a cloned
# repo and its .env can silently repoint inference — OPENAI_BASE_URL included —
# with your credential attached to the request. For a distributed CLI that is a
# credential-disclosure vector, not a convenience.
#
# Configure the tool instead, in precedence order:
#
#   1. flags                  yousim --port 8080
#   2. the shell environment  PROVIDER=groq yousim
#   3. ./.yousim.json         per-repo, provider and model ONLY (see below)
#   4. ~/.yousim/config.json
#   5. ~/.yousim/.env
#
# ─── Per-repo settings: ./.yousim.json ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# Commit this next to your project when a repo should use a particular model:
#
#   { "provider": "openrouter", "model": "nousresearch/hermes-3-llama-3.1-70b" }
#
# provider and model are the only keys accepted. A credential and an endpoint
# are properties of your machine, not of a repo, so "apiKey" and "baseURL" are
# refused — and refused loudly, with the reason, rather than ignored.
#
# ─── Machine-level settings: ~/.yousim/.env ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything below belongs there, not here. Same syntax.
#
#   PROVIDER            anthropic | openrouter | openai | groq
#   MODEL               Model id. Provider-specific, and it applies to EVERY
#                       provider, so a name set for one leaks to the next.
#                       Model choice dominates output quality: older, less
#                       instruction-tuned models simulate far better than
#                       current frontier assistants, which are trained out of
#                       exactly the loose associative generation this needs.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   Only the one matching PROVIDER is used, and they are
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  not interchangeable — OPENAI_API_KEY will not
#   OPENAI_API_KEY      authenticate OpenRouter.
#   GROQ_API_KEY
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL     Any OpenAI-compatible server (vLLM, Ollama, a gateway).
#                       Used only when PROVIDER=openai; most such servers want
#                       a non-empty OPENAI_API_KEY even though they ignore it.
#   YOUSIM_DB           Database path. Defaults to ~/.yousim/yousim.db.
#   YOUSIM_HOME         Move the config and data directory outright.
#   YOUSIM_KEYCHAIN=0   Never use the macOS Keychain; use the 0600 file.
#
# XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME are honored when set, and an existing
# ~/.yousim is migrated into them rather than orphaned.
#
# ─── What this file is still for ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Running this repo's dev servers directly (`bun run dev`), which are ordinary
# Bun/Vite processes and do read ./.env. Copy to .env and set these:

PORT=3000
# Only needed if the frontend and API are served from different origins.
VITE_API_URL=
